      "side": 1,
      "message": "This searcher only applies if the input string is \"self\" or \"me\" (see the \"matches\" method above in l. 335). \"self\"/\"me\" matches the account of the current user, but we only have a current user if asUser.isIdentifiedUser() is true. Otherwise it\u0027s an anonymous request and we don\u0027t know the account of the caller or they don\u0027t have one. This means when there is no current user (asUser.isIdentifiedUser() is false) then there is no match for \"self\"/\"me\".\n\nI included the input (\"self\"/\"me\") into the log now. I omitted it before because the input is not used for the matching in the search method.\n\nDone.",
